  "description": "The third READ reports '23', no record found. '23' is a perfectly ordinary branch in the online programs, which test DFHRESP(NOTFND) explicitly, and it is fatal here - which is the whole point of the case. CBACT03C tests exactly two statuses, '00' at :94 and '10' at :98, so a recognised-elsewhere status still reaches :101, still moves 12, and still abends at :113. Eight lines and RETURN-CODE 12. A translation that reused a shared status vocabulary and treated '23' as a benign not-found would silently turn an abend into a clean run.",
